      id: "course-y3-hum-w11-d4",
      dayNumber: 4,
      titleEn: "Uncle's Fishing Boat",
      titleMy: "ဦးလေး၏ ငါးဖမ်းလှေ",
      kind: LessonKind.reading,
      xpReward: 10,
      readingPassage: ReadingPassageModel(
        titleEn: "Uncle's Fishing Boat",
        titleMy: "ဦးလေး၏ ငါးဖမ်းလှေ",
        passageEn:
            "Kaung Sett's uncle lived in a small town along the Rakhine Coast, where the Bay of Bengal stretched out to the horizon every morning. \"Wake up early,\" his uncle said the night before, \"we sail out with the sunrise.\"\n\n"
            "The next morning, Kaung Sett helped push the wooden boat into the water as his uncle checked the large fishing nets. \"We're after shrimp today,\" his uncle explained, casting the net far out into the waves. Hours later, they hauled it back, wriggling with silver fish and pink shrimp.\n\n"
            "Back on shore, Kaung Sett noticed a group of visitors setting up beach chairs nearby, laughing as they built sandcastles. \"Do visitors come here often?\" he asked. \"All the time,\" his uncle laughed. \"They come for the beaches, and their money helps our whole town — hotels, restaurants, even the shop where we buy our nets.\"\n\n"
            "As they sorted the catch into baskets for the market, Kaung Sett looked out at the wide blue sea. \"So the coast gives us fish to eat and sell, and visitors who bring money too,\" he said. His uncle nodded. \"The sea gives generously, if we take care of it.\" Kaung Sett watched the waves roll in, understanding for the first time just how much his uncle's coastal town depended on the sea.",
        passageMy:
            "ကောင်းစက်၏ ဦးလေးသည် ဘင်္ဂလားပင်လယ်အော် နေ့စဉ်နံနက် အစွန်းအထိ ကျယ်ဝန်းသွားသော ရခိုင်ကမ်းရိုးတန်းတစ်လျှောက်ရှိ မြို့ငယ်တစ်မြို့တွင် နေထိုင်ခဲ့သည်။ \"မနက်ခင်းလင်းလင်းနိုးထ\" ဟု ညနေက ဦးလေး ပြောခဲ့သည်။ \"ငါတို့ နေထွက်ချိန်နဲ့အတူ ထွက်ကြမယ်။\"\n\n"
