      titleEn: "The Story of the First Settlers",
      titleMy: "ပထမဆုံး အခြေချသူများ၏ ဇာတ်လမ်း",
      kind: LessonKind.reading,
      xpReward: 10,
      readingPassage: ReadingPassageModel(
        titleEn: "The Story of the First Settlers",
        titleMy: "ပထမဆုံး အခြေချသူများ၏ ဇာတ်လမ်း",
        passageEn:
            "One evening, Kaung Sett's grandmother told him the story of how their town began, a tale passed down through many generations of their family. \"Long, long ago,\" she began, \"a small group of farming families traveled far in search of good land.\"\n\n"
            "\"They finally stopped beside a wide river,\" she continued, \"because the water was perfect for growing rice, and boats could carry goods to other towns.\" Kaung Sett imagined the very first families building simple huts along the riverbank, exactly where his own home now stood.\n\n"
            "\"Over many, many years, more families joined them,\" his grandmother said, \"and slowly, a small settlement grew into the township we live in today.\" She pointed out the window toward the old monastery on the hill. \"That monastery was one of the very first buildings the settlers built, hundreds of years ago.\"\n\n"
            "\"Is this story written down anywhere?\" Kaung Sett asked. \"Some of it,\" his grandmother said, \"but much of it has only ever been told out loud, passed from grandparent to grandchild, generation after generation.\" Kaung Sett realized that by listening carefully tonight, he had just become part of that very same chain, ready to tell the story again himself one day.",
        passageMy:
